rea search — Search every analyzed string or procedure name

Usage: rea search <path> [pattern] [options]

Arguments:
  path     App or program path
  pattern  Literal text or regex pattern

Options:
  --pattern <string>                          Complete literal text or regex pattern; use --pattern=<value> for leading dashes
  --kind <strings|procedures>                 Analyzed item kind to search (default: strings)
  --mode <literal|regex>                      Interpret the pattern as literal text or a regex (default: literal)
  --case-sensitive                            Match the pattern with exact letter case
  --snapshot <string>                         Load and update a local analysis snapshot
  --target-format <dos-com|raw-binary>        Explicit headerless interpretation (dos-com or raw-binary); omission preserves header-based detection
  --architecture <6502|x86|x86_64|arm|arm64>  Caller-supplied CPU family; required with --target-format raw-binary
  --entry-point <string>                      Caller-supplied load and entry address (0xhex); required with --target-format raw-binary
  --provider <value>                          Bind deep analysis to a provider ID or use deterministic auto selection

Global Options:
  --filter-output <keys>              Filter output by key paths (e.g. foo,bar.baz,a[0,3])
  --format <toon|json|yaml|md|jsonl>  Output format
  --full-output                       Show full output envelope
  --help                              Show help
  --llms, --llms-full                 Print LLM-readable manifest
  --schema                            Show JSON Schema for command
