0x14031d760	ego-browser import - Import browser data <NL>  <NL> Usage: <NL>   ego-browser import list <NL>   ego-browser import --browser <browser> [--profile <dir-name> ...] <NL>                  [--browser <browser> [--profile <dir-name> ...] ...] <NL>                  [--clear-existing-profiles] [--no-default] <NL>  <NL> Runs browser data import through the browser-side CLI service. <NL>  <NL> Options: <NL>   --browser <browser>       Start a browser import block <NL>   --profile <dir-name>      Import only the matching source profile directory <NL>                             Accepts multiple directory names until the next <NL>                             option; applies to the most recent browser block <NL>   --clear-existing-profiles  Remove all existing Ego profiles after a successful <NL>                             import, including Default and earlier imports <NL>   --no-default              Do not set Ego as the default browser after import <NL>  <NL> Subcommands: <NL>   list                       List detected importable browsers and profiles <NL>  <NL> Current support: <NL>   chrome                     Import from Google Chrome <NL>   edge                       Import from Microsoft Edge <NL>   brave                      Import from Brave <NL>  <NL> Notes: <NL>   Run `ego-browser import list` to see the exact browsers and profiles <NL>   detected on this machine. <NL>   The profile value must be the source profile directory name, such as <NL>   `Default`. <NL>   When `--browser` is used, each `--profile` group belongs to the most recent <NL>   browser block. <NL>   `--clear-existing-profiles` restarts Ego to apply imported data and clear all <NL>   old profiles. A failed or canceled import keeps existing profiles. <NL>   UI imports with clearExistingProfiles=true use the same clearing behavior. <NL>   Normal incremental imports add new profiles without restart. <NL>  <NL> Examples: <NL>   ego-browser import list <NL>   ego-browser import --browser brave