Need to inspect whether `ego-browser.exe` uses Chromium's Mojo invitation through `--ego-server-name` -> named mojo channel? The strings say "Failed to extract Mojo message pipe from invitation" and "ConnectToBootstrapLoop". The `--ego-server-name` is likely the Mojo server name used in the invitation. Allowed characters 64 ASCII `[A-Za-z0-9-_.]`. That's the closest to a "pipe name constant". We should report: no fixed pipe name; server name passed via `--ego-server-name` (validated 1-64 chars `[A-Za-z0-9._-]`), and bootstrap via Mojo invitation over a message pipe extracted from the invitation. The actual transport is likely Mojo's named pipe on Windows, but we don't have the exact name. We should be careful: Mojo on Windows uses named pipes internally with random names; the server name may be used for the invitation channel. Static evidence doesn't show exact pipe path.

