  @3252465: resulting application state.
  @3252495: ## Files and requests
  @3252518: Set an existing file input with absolute paths:
  @3252567: ```js
  @3252573: await page.setInputFiles("input[type=file]", ["/absolute/path/report.pdf"]);
  @3252650: ```
  @3252655: If a click creates the file input, start waiting before the click:
  @3252723: ```js
  @3252729: const chooserPromise = page.waitForFileChooser({ timeout: 10_000 });
  @3252798: await page.click("button.upload");
  @3252833: const chooser = await chooserPromise;
  @3252871: const result = await chooser.setFiles("/absolute/path/report.pdf");
  @3252939: ```
  @3252944: An upload-triggered JavaScript dialog may be returned as `result.dialog`; when
  @3253023: present, handle it with the dialog methods above.
  @3253074: For a browser download, arm the event before the triggering action and save the
  @3253154: returned artifact to an absolute path in the same script:
  @3253213: ```js
  @3253219: const downloadPromise = page.waitForEvent("download", { timeout: 30_000 });
  @3253295: await page.click("button.download");
  @3253332: const download = await downloadPromise;
  @3253372: console.log({
  @3253386:   url: download.url(),
  @3253409:   suggestedFilename: download.suggestedFilename(),
  @3253460: });
  @3253464: await download.saveAs("/absolute/path/report.pdf");
  @3253516: ```
  @3253521: `download.saveAs()` waits for completion and creates missing parent
  @3253589: directories. `download.path()` returns the round-local temporary file;
  @3253660: `failure()`, `cancel()`, and `delete()` manage its lifecycle. Temporary download
  @3253741: files are removed when the SDK round is disposed, so call `saveAs()` before the
  @3253821: script ends. Do not set a global download directory with raw CDP; each download
  @3253901: wait configures and restores only the addressed Page session.
  @3253964: `page.fetch()` runs `window.fetch()` in the Page: relative URLs, cookies, and
  @3254042: service workers use that Page, and browser CORS still applies. It returns
  @3254116: `{ ok, status, statusText, url, headers, body }`:
  @3254167: ```js
  @3254173: const response = await page.fetch("/api/items", {
  @3254223:   method: "POST",
  @3254241:   headers: { "content-type": "application/json" },
  @3254292:   body: JSON.stringify({ limit: 20 }),
  @3254331:   timeout: 10_000,
  @3254350: });
  @3254354: ```
  @3254359: Save binary responses without converting them to text:
  @3254415: ```js
  @3254421: await page.fetch("/image.png", { saveAs: "/absolute/path/image.png" });
  @3254493: ```
  @3254498: Use standard Node.js `fetch()` for background requests that do not need Page
  @3254575: browser semantics.
  @3254595: ## User control and completion
  @3254627: Stop when the user takes control or the space is inactive or unassigned. Do not
  @3254707: retry or route around the stop. Permission prompts, device choosers, and
  @3254780: other browser-owned prompts require the user to handle them.
  @3254842: When the user must act in the browser, call `await task.handOff()`, end the
  @3254918: round, and explain what they should do. After the user confirms, resume the
  @3254994: same space:
  @3255007: ```js
  @3255013: const task = await takeOverTaskSpace(7);
  @3255054: const userPage = task.userPage();
  @3255088: ```
