  @3255175: script must wait in place. Claim a user-owned or inactive space only when the
  @3255253: user explicitly asks; this includes a space you finished with kept Pages, which
  @3255333: `takeOverTaskSpace()` cannot resume. Find its numeric id first; names may be
  @3255410: duplicated. `listTaskSpaces()` entries expose that id as `id` (`spaceId` exists
  @3255490: only on a TaskSpace handle), so pass `entry.id` to `claimTaskSpace()` or
