33371: - Some internal page operations may use CDP under the hood via `NodeCdpChannel` (the interface name literally says Node-CDP channel; `sendCDPMessage`). But the exposed automation protocol is a custom JS API over Mojo; CDP is an escape hatch (`page.cdp()` / `task.cdp()` / `ego.sendCDPMessage`).
33372: - The custom API messages are serialized Mojo messages, not JSON text over WebSocket. JSON appears in `sendCDPMessage` example and in `snapshot` fields.
33373: - No fixed listen port for the browser automation channel; no WebSocket listener for CLI. `ego-browser.exe` imports only KERNEL32/ntdll/WINMM, no WS2_32/WINHTTP. So it cannot open a TCP socket itself (although Mojo named pipes may be used via kernel32). That's a decisive proof that CLI↔browser is not TCP WebSocket.
